            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0360" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 P. W./343: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-29T18:00:00+09:00">July 29, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 29—9:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1118. My 1103, July 27, 7 p.m. During a talk today the Chief of the American
                    Bureau of the Foreign Office informed Dooman that the Foreign Office had
                    received a very brief telegram from Admiral Nomura concerning the President’s
                    proposal but he characterized the report as being too brief to be of any use and
                    said that the Minister had instructed Nomura by telegraph on Sunday afternoon,
                    July 27, to submit promptly a comprehensive report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
